#X text 9 8 INFORMATION;
#X text 50 38 This is where the canvases for various headers and organizing graphics found throughout the patch get set. This is facilitated by a local subpatch called [pd canvas-ctrl]., f 187;
#X text 49 68 This subpatch contains a GUI to set all the canvas parameters (which is exposed for the "Title" field). Canvas values can be sent as a (very long) list to the object as well. The subpatch doesn't have [savestate] capabilities \, so currently the only way to save canvas parameters is through the list, f 187;
#X text 49 108 You can also click on the object box [pd how-to-use-canvas-ctrl] to see how to properly set values with messages., f 160;
#X obj 225 549 r mainColor_\$0;
#X obj 179 283 inlet;
#X text 222 281 Main Title Bar Color;
#X obj 179 339 s mainColor_\$0;
#X msg 179 309 bgclr \$1;
#X text 49 198 To keep all of my various patches uniform \, I tend to only change the main title (obviously) \, the color of the main title bar \, and the width of all the headers in the patch. Here I make these parameters accessible via inlets to this subpatch \, everything else is "hard-coded" internally. I could change these parameters via the messages below \, but this method is faster. These parameters get set AFTER the parameters set in the lists below \, so they over-ride the lists. I use a [loadbang] outside this subpatch to ensure the desired value gets sent every time the patch is opened., f 185;
